<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates rise across the board.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates rise across the board.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose slightly in all maturities on a technical correction, dealers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Interest rates have reached bottom,&quot; a foreign bank trader said.</p>
<p>Banks were also sourcing their pesos from PHIBOR which had lower rates and investing them in higher yielding T-bills, she said.</p>
<p>This led to an upward adjustment in PHIBOR rates.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 13		 FEB 12</p>
<p>    1 W		10			9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/8		 10  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/8		 10  1/16</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  5/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  3/8</p>
<p>    VAL		14-Feb		  13-Feb</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
